    <string name="onb1_title">Be on the same network as your Apple TV</string>
    <string name="onb1_body">Make sure your phone and Apple TV are on the same Wi-Fi network. Devices on different networks can’t see each other.</string>
    <string name="onb2_title">Prefer a 5 GHz connection</string>
    <string name="onb2_body">Connect to the 5 GHz band in your Wi-Fi settings for a smoother picture and lower latency.</string>
    <string name="onb3_title">Stay close to the router</string>
    <string name="onb3_body">The closer your phone is to the router, the smoother the picture. Walls and distance weaken the signal.</string>
    <string name="onb4_title">Connect Apple TV with a cable</string>
    <string name="onb4_body">For best performance, connect your Apple TV to the router with an Ethernet cable.</string>
    <string name="onb5_title">Choose what to share</string>
    <string name="onb5_body">When you start, Android will ask what to share. Choose “%1$s” and mirroring continues as you move between apps. With “%2$s” only that app is shown. We recommend sharing the entire screen.</string>
    <string name="onb6_title">DRM-protected apps can’t be mirrored!</string>
    <string name="onb6_body">Apps with content protection, like Netflix and Spotify, show a black screen or stay silent. Keep this in mind before making a purchase.</string>
    <string name="premium_title">Mirror without ads.</string>
    <string name="premium_body">All mirroring features stay free. The subscription only removes ads and the watermark.</string>
